Art Willis wrote:
> 
> [Problem compiling with the Qt library.]
>
> ...macro "yn" passed 2 arguments, but takes just 1

	I dimly remember seeing that error message before.  I googled
for "macro yn passed", and got two hits.  Pat Rankin gave the fix:

>     Edit win/Qt/qt_win.cpp and insert
>
> #undef yn
>
> prior to the `#include "qt_win.h"' line.
>
>    NetHack has a macro named yn() that's set up by hack.h, but one
> of the Qt V3 header files has a different macro attempting to use the
> same name.  Fortunately qt_win.cpp doesn't need either of them, so
> simply removing one before it conflicts with the other will solve the
> problem.

	(Since at least three people have hit this, perhaps qt_win.cpp
should be changed for the next release.)

